From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ar <sm64ar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Story mode and game flow

Seams the host uses to run the game's flow, all inert without gArMode:

- gArStory runs the title screen, file select, act selector and the vanilla
  game flow (entry script, Start, attract demo); gArScreen says which screen
  is up and returns to LEVEL when a level is cleared. The act selector
  exposes a pick seam so the host can choose an act.
- initiate_warp and the game-over path offer each warp to the host first
  (before_warp, game_over); a warp the host handles makes the game skip its
  own follow-ups.
- the level script's MARIO_POS is recorded on every level load, before any
  warp moves Mario, so the host can put that floor on the table top.
- there is no save prompt: a star or key is saved at once ("Save &
  Continue") and each such save is reported to the host.
